            <ArticleTitle>Intra cardiac mass--a diagnostic and therapeutic dilemma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>373-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="AIM" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">We report an unusual case of previously healthy post partum woman who had presented with congestive cardiac failure. She had no significant past history.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHOD" NlmCategory="METHODS">She underwent cardiac evaluation. Echo showed severe left ventricular dysfunction and multiple mobile masses in the left ventricle. Cardiac MRI was done to assess the intracardiac mass.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULT" NlmCategory="RESULTS">Cardiac MRI helped in differentiating clot from intra cardiac tumor. She was effectively treated with anticoagulants.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Cardiac MRI is a useful investigative modality to differentiate intracardiac tumor and clot and helps in guiding the management.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
